WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.600
 As our learners work through assignments,  

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.600
 it can be helpful 
  to check on their progress 

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.040
 as well as see their code 
  in a working environment 

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.040
 in order to help them troubleshoot 
  any issues that they're having. 

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.160
 And we can do all of that from within 
  RStudio Cloud. For this walk through 

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.000
 I've added myself as a learner 
  to our data visualization workspace, 

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.920
 which we can confirm 
  by clicking on the members tab. 

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.120
 There are two ways to access learner work. 

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.560
 One is to click on an individual's name 
  from the members tab. 

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.120
 When we do this, 
  we're taken to our learner's projects. 

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.720
 In this case, our learner has only worked 
  on assignment one. 

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.720
 But we can click into their work 
  and see what they've created, 

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.040
 as well as run their code. 

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.280
 It's important to note that when we open 
  a learner's project in RStudio Cloud, 

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.040
 we are not creating a separate 
  copy of the work -- 

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.080
 we're directly accessing their work.  

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.960
 Any changes we make here will be 
  incorporated into the learner's project. 

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.960
 One advantage of this 
  is that we can write comments or provide 

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.880
 sample code for our learners 
  in an asynchronous manner. 

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.960
 Another point worth mentioning is that if 
  we as educators, or really anyone 

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.920
 with the moderator or administrative role 
  within the workspace, 

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.560
 opens a learners work while 
  the learner is working on it, 

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.480
 the learner will be disconnected 
  from their project. 

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.720
 It may be helpful 
  to let learners know that this may happen, 

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.960
 especially if you and your learners 
  are working asynchronously. 

